at least two people have died in a fire  at an overcrowded Greek migrant camp the  dead are reported to be a woman and a  child that blaze struck the Moria camp  on the island of Lesbos it was later put  out but residents of the camp angry at  what they say was a slow response  clashed with police  now conditions at the camp are at a  breaking point after a sharp spike in  migrant arrivals from turkey misery upon  misery on the Greek island of Lesbos  migrants scrambled to escape a cloud of  tear gas fired by police as a tragic  chain of events unfolded at the Moria  camp a fire broke out inside the camp  quickly spreading through containers  used to house residents there are  conflicting reports about what happened  next an NGO working in the camp says a  group of migrants rushed to extinguish  the blaze and police used tear gas to  chase them away  police say they fired tear gas to  disperse rioters angered by the time it  took to preside the deadly fire  what's undisputed is that a group of  migrants attacked firefighters who  arrived on the scene a video posted on  Facebook shows the damage additional  police officers were flown in from  Athens to help restore calm conditions  at Moria have always been difficult but  in recent months they've gotten worse  migrant arrivals to Greece from Turkey  have surged reaching their highest level  since 2016 when the European Union  signed a deal with Ankara to stem the  flow about 12,000 people are currently  housed in the camp though it's only  designed for a quarter that number the  deadly fire and rioting will increase  pressure on the Greek government to ease  the situation with the harsh winter  months approaching fast  let's go straight to Athens now we're  joined by correspondent aunty Kurosawa  good morning to you auntie do we know  anything more about what might have  caused this fire at the Marea camp well  there are conflicting reports as to what  in fact caused this blaze there by one  account it was caused in fact by this  woman who was was killed in this place  because she started cooking in her  container and that quickly spread by  other accounts there were two separate  fires one fire that was set outside the  camp and then within 20 minutes another  fire set within the camp which kind of  shows an orchestrated and premeditated  kind of attempt either way the chaos  that kind of ensued and what happened  simply underscores the abysmal situation  in what is being called Europe's most  embarrassing refugee camp 13,000 people  crammed in a camp build to hold 3,000  yea abysmal is the right word with the  images were getting show just how over  crowded this campus can you tell  something about about the riots as a  result of this fire well the the riots  affectionately what happened would  ensued was that once these these fires  took took place many of the refugees who  were in there and who have been  extremely frustrated by very long stays  simply rioted because of the asylum  process that is taking so long that  however as far as rescue attempts had  had a very negative impact because the  fire fighters could not move in and and  eventually the police riot police had to  move in and fire some tear gas to  disperse these militant migrants and to  bring about some calm and to get this  rescue operation going eventually the  fire was doused out by water planes and  there is some degree of calmness  at this camp but there are great fears  among the locals that it's just a matter  of time before new riots will be  triggered anti-corrosive earth air force  in Athens
 

